    "actual_stdout_custody": "Actual qualified F25 first creates fresh spec.out with mkdir, attests owned scope, records all inputs, takes nonblocking global compiler lock, and opens per-command stdout/stderr in binary wb under that fresh output. subprocess stdout is that file descriptor; C.compact bytearray is written without text reencoding. F25 reads rawstdout afterward without replacing it; its JSON command row goes to controllerstdout, not commandstdout. Unique reviewed step names are required because wb itself permits duplicate-name overwrite.",
    "bounded_return": "Actual C.compact token/aggregate checks enforce <=8MiB before buffer extension; returned bytearray is valid binary-write input. The entry does not print other stdout. Exact actual stderr/exit and whole unsigned JSON/inputSHA/bytebound independent readback must qualify capture; no Rust passed0 field can establish model acceptance.",
